IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Social Security Act -- what the other modules share: the answer types, calendar months, attaining an age, and the parties
-- and acts of the regulative rules. Nothing here is a rule of the Act except where a section is cited.

§ `Answers`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A question that can reach a gap answers `not covered`, with the reason.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- 90 FR 49047 sets the bend points, exempt amounts and other figures for 2026 only; no other year's notice is deposited.
    `the figures the Act needs for that year are not deposited: only the 2026 Federal Register notices are`
    -- s 415(a)(1) applies to those first eligible (or dying) after 1978; s 415(a)(4)-(5) and (d) keep older rules for others.
    `the person was first eligible, or died, before 1979, so the old PIA rules in s 415(a)(4), (5) and (d) apply, which are not encoded`
    -- A PIA first computed for an earlier year is increased by each year's s 415(i) cost-of-living increase. The increases for
    -- years before 2026 are not deposited.
    `the PIA of a person first eligible before 2026 has been raised by cost-of-living increases that are not deposited`
    -- s 416(i)(3)(B)(iii), s 423(c)(1)(B)(iii): the second young-worker rule, for a person who had an earlier period of
    -- disability before 31.
    `insured status after an earlier period of disability that began before age 31 (s 423(c)(1)(B)(iii)) is not encoded`
    -- s 1382c(f): the income and resources of an ineligible spouse living with the individual, or of a parent living with a
    -- child under 18, are deemed to be the individual's. The deeming rules are not encoded.
    `deeming of an ineligible spouse's or parent's income and resources (s 1382c(f)) is not encoded`
    -- s 1382(e)(1)(B): the reduced rate for a couple in a medical treatment facility.
    `the reduced rate in a medical treatment facility is encoded only for an individual without an eligible spouse`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

-- A benefit question has three answers: an amount, no benefit (with the reason the Act gives), or not covered.
DECLARE `Benefit answer` IS ONE OF
    `a monthly benefit of`      HAS `dollars`  IS A NUMBER
    `no benefit`                HAS `reason`   IS A STRING
    `benefit not covered`       HAS `why`      IS A `Why not covered`

§ `Calendar months`

-- Months are counted as one number: year times 12, plus the month less one. January 2026 is 24312.
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month number of` `year` `month` MEANS `year` TIMES 12 PLUS `month` MINUS 1

DECLARE `Calendar month` HAS
    `year`  IS A NUMBER
    `month` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `month number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Calendar month`
`the calendar month numbered` `month number` MEANS
    `Calendar month` WITH
        `year`  IS FLOOR (`month number` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `month` IS `month number` MINUS (12 TIMES FLOOR (`month number` DIVIDED BY 12)) PLUS 1

GIVEN `month number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of month number` `month number` MEANS FLOOR (`month number` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- s 413(a)(1): a quarter ends on 31 March, 30 June, 30 September or 31 December. Quarters are numbered as months are.
GIVEN `month number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the quarter number of month` `month number` MEANS FLOOR (`month number` DIVIDED BY 3)

GIVEN `date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month number of the date` `date` MEANS `the month number of` (DATE_YEAR `date`) (DATE_MONTH `date`)

§ `Attaining an age`

-- The Act says "attains age 62" and so on without defining when an age is attained. NOTES.md finding 1: the rule taken here
-- is the common-law rule that the Social Security Administration applies by regulation (20 CFR 404.2(c)(4), not deposited):
-- an age is attained on the day before the birthday. It moves the month only for a person born on the 1st of a month, who
-- attains each age on the last day of the month before. Change this one rule to count from the birthday itself.
GIVEN `birth date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month in which age 0 is attained` `birth date` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `birth date` EQUALS 1
        THEN `the month number of the date` `birth date` MINUS 1
        ELSE `the month number of the date` `birth date`

GIVEN `birth date` IS A DATE, `age in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month in which the age in months is attained` `birth date` `age in months` MEANS
    `the month in which age 0 is attained` `birth date` PLUS `age in months`

GIVEN `birth date` IS A DATE, `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month in which age is attained` `birth date` `age` MEANS
    `the month in which the age in months is attained` `birth date` (`age` TIMES 12)

GIVEN `birth date` IS A DATE, `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year in which age is attained` `birth date` `age` MEANS
    `the year of month number` (`the month in which age is attained` `birth date` `age`)

-- s 402(a)(B) and others say "the first month throughout which" a person is a given age. That is the month the age is
-- attained only if it is attained on the 1st of the month (a person born on the 2nd); otherwise it is the next month.
GIVEN `birth date` IS A DATE, `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first month throughout which the age is attained` `birth date` `age` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `birth date` EQUALS 2
        THEN `the month in which age is attained` `birth date` `age`
        ELSE `the month in which age is attained` `birth date` `age` PLUS 1

§ `Rounding`

-- s 415(a)(1)(A), s 403(a)(1): "rounded, if not a multiple of $0.10, to the next lower multiple of $0.10".
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded down to a multiple of 10 cents` `amount` MEANS FLOOR (`amount` TIMES 10) DIVIDED BY 10

-- s 402(q)(8): a reduction "not a multiple of $0.10 ... shall be increased to the next higher multiple of $0.10".
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded up to a multiple of 10 cents` `amount` MEANS CEILING (`amount` TIMES 10) DIVIDED BY 10

-- s 415(g): a monthly benefit "not a multiple of $1 shall be rounded to the next lower multiple of $1".
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded down to a whole dollar` `amount` MEANS FLOOR `amount`

§ `Parties and acts of the regulative rules`

-- The actors the text names. The individual is the person in the seat; officials appear only for what they owe that person.
DECLARE `SSA party` IS ONE OF
    `the individual`
    `the Commissioner of Social Security`

DECLARE `SSA act` IS ONE OF
    -- s 403(h)(1)(A)
    `report earnings for the taxable year to the Commissioner`
    -- s 405(b)(1), s 1383(c)(1)
    `request a hearing on the determination`
    -- s 405(g)
    `commence a civil action to review the final decision`
    -- s 402(i)
    `file an application for the lump-sum death payment`
    -- s 1382(e)(2)
    `take all appropriate steps to apply for and obtain the other payments`
    -- s 1383(e)(1)-(2)
    `report the event or change in circumstances`
    -- s 1383(c)(2)
    `make the determination on the basis of the hearing`
    -- s 1395p(d), (e), (i)
    `enroll in Part B`
